Title: The Tell-Tale Heart

Credit: Written by

Author: Author

Source: Adapted from book

Draft date: 7/30/2026

FADE IN:

INT. DIM STUDY - NIGHT

A single candle flickers over a worn desk. The room is shadowed and intimate. NARRATOR sits before the camera, eyes intense.

NARRATOR

(True!—nervous—very, very dreadfully nervous I had been and am. But why will you say that I am mad? The disease had sharpened my senses.)

NARRATOR (CONT’D)

My hearing is acute; I heard all things in heaven and on earth… even things in hell. Listen, and observe how calmly I can tell you this whole story.

  
INT. OLD MAN’S CHAMBER - NIGHT

In the dark, a trembling OLD MAN sleeps soundly in a modest bed. The room is small, furnished sparsely. A dark lantern, clutched in trembling hands, casts a narrow beam through an almost-open door.

NARRATOR (V.O.)

I loved the old man. He had never wronged me. But his eye—the eye of a vulture, that pale blue eye with a film over it—haunted me. My blood ran cold whenever it fell upon me.

  
INT. OLD MAN’S CHAMBER - NIGHT

The door’s latch turns silently. NARRATOR, face obscured in shadow, slowly pushes his head into the room. The soft, creeping sound of the lantern’s mechanism and the creak of hinges punctuate the silence.

OLD MAN (O.S.)

(whispered, startled) Who’s there?

A flicker of movement; NARRATOR freezes, every muscle tensed. For an agonizing hour, he remains immobile as the OLD MAN listens, uncomprehending in the dark.

NARRATOR (V.O.)

And then, on the eighth night, a slight groan—a groan of mortal terror. I opened a tiny crevice in the lantern and let a single dim ray fall upon that accursed eye.

  
INT. OLD MAN’S CHAMBER - NIGHT

In the oppressive blackness, the narrow beam illuminates the OLD MAN’s vulture-eye. NARRATOR’s eyes burn with feverish intensity.

NARRATOR (V.O.)

It was open—wide open. Fury surged through me like a drumbeat, a beating heart that grew louder with each pulse.

Suddenly, with a loud yell, NARRATOR hurls the lantern wide open and leaps into the room.

The OLD MAN shrieks—a single, piercing sound. In one swift moment, NARRATOR drags the OLD MAN from his bed. The heavy bed is toppled over him as chaos collides with cold, deliberate intent.

NARRATOR (CONT’D, softly triumphant)

I smiled gaily, for the deed was so far done. And yet, even as his heart beat a muffled rhythm, the sound spoke of a terrible, relentless noise.

  
INT. OLD MAN’S CHAMBER - LATER NIGHT

The room lies still and oppressive. NARRATOR, now alone, approaches the lifeless body. With grim precision he dismembers the corpse—cutting off the head, pulling away the limbs.

NARRATOR (V.O.)

I took up planks from the chamber’s floor and concealed the evidence beneath the boards. No human eye, not even his, could have detected a thing.

He meticulously replaces the boards, leaving no trace of the horror just enacted. A dark tub glints at the side—a morbid receptacle for his work.

  
INT. FOYER - DAWN

Pale morning light seeps through a grimy window. Three officers—OFFICER REYNOLDS, OFFICER MERRICK, and OFFICER DAVIS—stand in the entryway. Their faces are composed, their manners courteous.

NARRATOR

(with an eerie cheerfulness)

Good morning, gentlemen. I welcome you. The shriek you heard, if I may explain, was but a dream. The old man, you see, is absent on business.

He leads them slowly through the house, pausing in the dim corridor, then finally toward the old man’s chamber.

  
INT. OLD MAN’S CHAMBER - DAWN

NARRATOR gestures to the room with a practiced air of hospitality. He displays the old man’s “treasures” as if on exhibition. Chairs are arranged casually. He then sits in a chair placed directly above the hidden corpse.

OFFICER REYNOLDS

(nodding cordially)

Everything appears in order, sir.

The officers chat amiably as NARRATOR’s confidence seems unshaken. Yet beneath his calm exterior, a faint, rhythmic sound begins to pulse.

  
INT. FOYER - DAWN

Alone with his thoughts and the company of the officers, NARRATOR paces. The persistent, low, dull thumping swells into an unbearable cadence. His voice rises in pitch and speed as anxiety consumes him.

NARRATOR

(voice trembling and growing louder)

Villains! Dissemble no more! I admit the deed! Tear up the planks! Here, here! It is the beating of his hideous heart!

He raves, gestures wildly, and swats at the air in a futile attempt to silence the sound. The officers exchange puzzled glances, their smiles fading into stern concern.

The heartbeat—louder, louder, louder—overwhelms him as his final confession echoes into the charged silence.

  
FADE OUT
